        "text": "{\"recorded_count\": 21, \"total_count\": 21, \"missing_ids\": [], \"complete\": true, \"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"FT-1\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Default sort by Priority groups all High tasks first, then Medium, then Low. After editing a task's priority from High to Low, it moved to the end of the list confirming live re-sort by priority.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-2\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Switching Sort by to Deadline reordered active tasks ascending: Sep 4, Sep 7, Sep 10, Sep 16.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-3\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Cannot modify content/priority of tasks with an incomplete prerequisite\", \"actual\": \"Per the spec, a task with an unmet prerequisite should still allow modification of description and priority fields. Instead, the Edit (pen) button is fully disabled (opacity-50, cursor-not-allowed) for such tasks (e.g. \\\"Complete tax filing\\\"), and clicking it does nothing - no edit dialog opens at all, so description and priority cannot be modified either. Editing only works for tasks without pending prerequisites.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-4\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created \\\"Test Task Alpha\\\" via Add Task dialog; toast \\\"Task created\\\" shown and task appeared in Active list, active count incremented 5->6.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Title \\\"Test Task Alpha\\\", Description \\\"This is a test description\\\", Deadline 2026-09-10 (displayed as \\\"Sep 10\\\") all saved and displayed correctly on the created task card.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edited task (title/description/priority saved, toast \\\"Task updated\\\"), marked a task complete (toast, moved to Completed tab), and deleted a task (toast \\\"Task deleted\\\", removed from list, counts updated).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked complete toggle on \\\"Schedule dentist appointment\\\"; it moved from Active (5) to Completed (3) tab, counts updated correctly (5 active/2 completed -> 5/3... verified via header text \\\"5 active, 3 completed\\\").\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Page loads by default on the \\\"Active\\\" tab, displaying only non-completed/ongoing tasks; a separate \\\"Completed\\\" tab holds finished tasks.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created a task with \\\"Buy groceries\\\" as a prerequisite (single); pre-existing \\\"Submit final report\\\" task shows \\\"2 prerequisites incomplete\\\" demonstrating multiple prerequisite binding works.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Tasks with incomplete prerequisites show disabled Edit and Complete buttons with classes \\\"cursor-not-allowed opacity-50\\\" / \\\"text-muted-foreground/40 cursor-not-allowed\\\" (visually grayed out). After the prerequisite (\\\"Buy groceries\\\") was completed, both buttons became enabled automatically.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Tasks with unmet prerequisites display a prominent label such as \\\"Prerequisite \\\\\\\"Review project proposal\\\\\\\" incomplete\\\" or \\\"2 prerequisites incomplete\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Complete toggle button for a task with unmet prerequisite is disabled and unclickable (Playwright click timed out: \\\"element is not enabled\\\"). After prerequisite was completed, the toggle became enabled.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"\\\"Buy groceries\\\" is a prerequisite of \\\"Test Task Alpha Edited\\\". Opening the Edit dialog for \\\"Buy groceries\\\" shows its Prerequisites checklist without \\\"Test Task Alpha Edited\\\" as an option, preventing the reverse/circular dependency.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"\\\"Create Task\\\" button remains disabled when the Title field is empty or contains only whitespace (\\\"   \\\"), preventing task creation without a title.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Deadline field is a native HTML5 input[type=date], which structurally enforces a valid YYYY-MM-DD date format; entered values (e.g. 2026-09-10) were always stored/displayed in correct ISO date format.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-16\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Past deadline dates are accepted without validation\", \"actual\": \"Entered deadline \\\"2020-01-01\\\" (a past date relative to current date 2026-09-02) in the Create Task form; the Create Task button remained enabled and the task was created successfully with a toast \\\"Task created\\\". The task then displayed with an \\\"Overdue: Jan 1\\\" label in the active list instead of being blocked from creation.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Completed tasks (\\\"Reply to client emails\\\", \\\"Organize desk\\\", \\\"Schedule dentist appointment\\\", \\\"Buy groceries\\\") remain visible under the \\\"Completed\\\" tab after being marked complete; they are not deleted and the completed count increments accordingly.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No details popup appears when hovering over a generic task\", \"actual\": \"Hovered over task cards without dependency badges (e.g. \\\"Review project proposal\\\", \\\"Test Task Alpha Edited\\\" heading, whole card container) - verified via DOM query for [role=\\\"tooltip\\\"] elements, none were rendered/visible. Only tasks displaying a dependency badge (\\\"Prerequisite incomplete\\\" / \\\"N prerequisite(s) completed\\\") show a tooltip on hover, but plain task hover produces no details pop-up.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"When the Title field is empty, the \\\"Create Task\\\" button is rendered in a disabled state (grayed out, non-interactive), providing clear visual feedback that a title is required.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Hovering over the \\\"Prerequisite incomplete\\\" badge or the \\\"N prerequisite(s) completed\\\" badge triggers a tooltip titled \\\"Dependency Chain\\\" listing each prerequisite task name and its status (e.g. \\\"Review project proposal - pending\\\", \\\"Buy groceries\\\" for a completed one).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each task card displays the title (heading), due date (e.g. \\\"Sep 4\\\", \\\"Tomorrow\\\", \\\"Overdue: Jan 1\\\"), and completion status is indicated both by tab placement (Active vs Completed) and by a distinct check-circle icon/button state per task.\"}]}"
