d deadline \"2020-01-01\" (a past date relative to current date 2026-09-02) in the Create Task form; the Create Task button remained enabled and the task was created successfully with a toast \"Task created\". The task then displayed with an \"Overdue: Jan 1\" label in the active list instead of being blocked from creation.\n\n- [X] CS-17: Tasks marked as completed should not be automatically deleted; they should remain visible.\n\n\n## Interaction\n- [ ] IX-18: A details pop-up window will appear when the user hovers over the task.\n  - Bug Report:\n    - Issue: No details popup appears when hovering over a generic task\n    - Actual: Hovered over task cards without dependency badges (e.g. \"Review project proposal\", \"Test Task Alpha Edited\" heading, whole card container) - verified via DOM query for [role=\"tooltip\"] elements, none were rendered/visible. Only tasks displaying a dependency badge (\"Prerequisite incomplete\" / \"N prerequisite(s) completed\") show a tooltip on hover, but plain task hover produces no details pop-up.\n\n- [X] IX-19: Provide visual feedback when creating a new to-do item without adding any title content.\n\n- [X] IX-20: Visual feedback when the user hovers over the dependency list.\n\n\n## Content\n- [X] CT-21: The main page must display the task title, due date, and completion status."
